      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets does the number $\\sqrt{0}$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we note that $\\sqrt{0}=0$ is zero.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}^{+}$ contains the positive integers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Z}^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ contains the negative rational numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}^{-}$ contains the negative integers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Z}^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ contains the positive integers (natural numbers). Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{N}$.\n\nTherefore, select none of the sets; leave every box unchecked.",
